{
  "_readme": [
    "Scenes for ./gradlew runRenders (-Ponly=<regex> renders just the matching ids; -Pstay keeps the game open after).",
    "Each scene is built with commands at its own spot (~ is the scene's origin), runs for 'wait' ticks, then only the blocks in 'region' (relative, inclusive; default just the origin) and the entities in it are drawn into docs/assets/renders/<id>.png.",
    "Blocks face south; yaw 135 / pitch 30 looks from the south-east, so you see the front on the left and the right-hand side. Helpers outside the region (motors, walls, burners) run the scene without being drawn.",
    "'block' fills {block} in the commands; 'variants' repeat the scene with another block, as <id>--<variant id> (the variant ids of the entry in docs/data).",
    "\"!use <item> x y z face\" (x y z as ~ offsets) has a fake player use the item on that face of that block, as a click would: for wires laid on a face and fittings clipped onto lines, which commands can't place properly."
  ],
  "supersample": 2,
  "pixelsPerBlock": 400,
  "maxSize": 1600,
  "iconSize": 128,
  "mysteries": ["comedymonkeysaddons:clockwork_juggernaut_spawn_egg", "comedymonkeysaddons:clockwork_juggernaut"],
  "spacing": 32,
  "defaults": {
    "yaw": 135,
    "pitch": 30,
    "wait": 60
  },
  "shots": [
